---
import RecipeLayout from '../../layouts/RecipeLayout.astro';
---
<RecipeLayout title="Brioche Base">
  <div class="recipe-title-block">
    <h1>Brioche Base</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Still proofing — check back soon.</p>
  </div>

  <main>
    <section class="block">
      <div class="callout">
        <p>This one's still in the oven, so to speak. The Brioche Base is one of the enriched-dough foundations behind Bruce's Breads' Enriched Doughs &amp; Laminated Pastries section — a stiff, white-flour-leaning levain (45–50% hydration, 40% of flour weight) softened directly into cold milk and eggs before the flour goes in, built specifically to carry butter, sugar, and egg without fighting the dough's structure.</p>
        <p>It's already been baked, tested, and approved — what's left is the full write-up: recipe card, step-by-step tutorial, ingredient history, and a baking playlist, the same full treatment every other recipe on this site gets. Once that's done, it'll live right here.</p>
        <p>In the meantime, the site's <a href="/guides/">baking Guides</a> have plenty on the technique behind it — the <a href="/guides/starter/starter-vs-levain/">Starter vs. Levain</a> guide covers why this base uses a stiff starter in the first place.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</RecipeLayout>
